## Frequently Asked Questions

### Does HealthSpring Medicare Advantage cover therapy?

Medicare covers many outpatient mental health services, including individual and group psychotherapy and certain family counseling. With Medicare Advantage, coverage and costs are administered through your specific plan, so you should confirm your individual benefits and network.

### How do I find HealthSpring Medicare Advantage providers for mental health care?

You can use HealthSpring's provider directory to search for participating providers. Look for behavioral health professionals and then confirm that the provider participates in your specific HealthSpring plan. HealthSpring provides plan-specific provider directories for members.

### Is Manahil Riaz a HealthSpring Medicare Advantage provider?

Manahil Riaz is listed as a Licensed Professional Counselor in HealthSpring's 2026 Texas and Oklahoma PPO provider directory under behavioral health providers. Because plan participation and directory information can change, confirm your specific plan before scheduling care.

### Can I use HealthSpring Medicare Advantage for counseling in Houston?

Potentially, depending on your specific plan, provider network, and covered benefits. Medicare covers a range of outpatient mental health services, but Medicare Advantage plans can have their own network and cost-sharing requirements.

### Does Medicare cover mental health counselors?

Yes. Medicare.gov lists mental health counselors among the professionals who may provide covered outpatient mental health services, subject to Medicare requirements and applicable state rules.

### Does HealthSpring cover online therapy?

Some mental health services can be provided through telehealth under Medicare, and Medicare covers certain mental health e-visits with eligible providers. However, HealthSpring plan-specific rules may apply, so confirm telehealth coverage with your plan and provider.

### What should I ask before seeing a HealthSpring therapist?

Ask whether the therapist is in-network with your exact plan, whether the service you need is covered, what your copay or coinsurance will be, whether a referral or authorization is required, and whether telehealth is covered if you prefer online sessions.

